      change to take effect. The one you have open keeps what it had until then.`)}),u(x,S)};y(L,x=>{var S;(S=s())!=null&&S.canRestart?x(B):x(I,!1)})}n(w),u(T,w)},$$slots:{icon:!0,footer:!0,default:!0}}),Fe()}yt(["click"]);var aU=v('<div class="note svelte-cbmkf3">Start the MCP server above to reveal your exact URL and token.</div>'),nU=v(`<p class="warn svelte-cbmkf3"><!> The relay is not installed yet, so setup is unavailable. It arrives with a Real update.
          Until then, connect manually with the URL and token below.</p>`),rU=v('<p class="warn svelte-cbmkf3"><!> The relay is not installed yet - it arrives with a Real update. Until then, use the URL and token below.</p>'),sU=v(`<div class="docs svelte-cbmkf3"><!> <p class="lead svelte-cbmkf3">Real hosts a local MCP server. Once connected, an AI client can inject, run Luau, read the
      console, search the game and its scripts, scan memory, spy on remotes, and drive the game with
      real input. Most tools need a client injected and in a game; a few (search-api, files,
      diagnostics, open-script, launch-roblox) work with Real alone.</p> <section class="svelte-cbmkf3"><h3 class="svelte-cbmkf3"><!> Connecting a client</h3> <p class="svelte-cbmkf3">Use the client list in the settings above. Real detects Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor,
        Codex, Grok, Antigravity, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, LM Studio, OpenClaw and ZCode, and sets each one up with a single click. A client reads this config when it
        launches, so restart it after connecting or disconnecting (the terminal CLIs, Claude Code,
        Grok and OpenCode, just need a new session) - a session already running keeps whatever it loaded until then.</p> <p class="hint svelte-cbmkf3">Codex is the coding side of the ChatGPT app, which is the only side that can reach a local
        server. Real appears under its MCP servers, not the chat "Apps" list, which accepts public
        HTTPS servers only.</p> <p class="hint svelte-cbmkf3">No access token is stored, so setup survives Real restarts and updates. A client marked
        "Needs repair" was added the old way, with a URL and token that expire on the next restart.</p> <!></section> <section class="svelte-cbmkf3"><h3 class="svelte-cbmkf3"><!> Any other client</h3> <p class="svelte-cbmkf3">For a client Real does not set up automatically, point it at the local relay. It is a plain
        stdio MCP server with no URL and no token, and it keeps working across Real restarts and
        updates because it resolves the live endpoint itself every time it runs - set it up once and
        never touch it again.</p> <div class="code svelte-cbmkf3"><code class="svelte-cbmkf3"> </code> <button class="svelte-cbmkf3"><!></button></div> <p class="hint svelte-cbmkf3">In a JSON config (Cursor, Claude Desktop and most others), add it under <code class="svelte-cbmkf3">mcpServers</code>:</p> <div class="code svelte-cbmkf3"><code class="block svelte-cbmkf3"> </code> <button class="svelte-cbmkf3"><!></button></div> <!> <p class="hint svelte-cbmkf3" style="margin-top:10px;">Prefer HTTP? Real also serves at the address below with a fixed token that survives restarts.
        The relay is still the better choice: an HTTP entry breaks if the port is ever taken and Real
        has to fall back to another, whereas the relay follows the port automatically.</p> <div class="code svelte-cbmkf3"><code class="svelte-cbmkf3"> </code> <button class="svelte-cbmkf3"><!></button></div> <div class="code svelte-cbmkf3"><code class="svelte-cbmkf3"> </code> <button class="svelte-cbmkf3"><!></button></div> <p class="hint svelte-cbmkf3">Send the token as an <code class="svelte-cbmkf3">Authorization: Bearer</code> header.</p></section> <section class="svelte-cbmkf3"><h3 class="svelte-cbmkf3"><!> Permissions</h3> <p class="svelte-cbmkf3">Every capability (Inject, Execute, Scripts, Instances, Memory, Game knowledge, Console, Remote spy, Files,
        Input, Screenshot, Diagnostics) is a toggle above. Turn one off and its tools are refused
        immediately. Execute and Input let the AI run code and drive input, so review them.</p></section> <section class="svelte-cbmkf3"><h3 class="svelte-cbmkf3"><!> What the AI can do</h3> <p class="svelte-cbmkf3">The full toolset your AI client gets once connected. Most tools read or act on the running
        game; the last group drives Real itself.</p> <ul class="tools svelte-cbmkf3"><li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">API reference</b>: search-api (every Real global and library with signatures and docs, plus notes on Real's quirks; works with no client injected, so the AI can check what exists before writing Luau)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Clients</b>: list-clients (injected clients and their game), set-active-client, inject</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Execute</b>: get-data-by-code (run Luau, get back what it printed and returned), eval (evaluate one expression), execute and execute-file (fire-and-forget, for loops that keep running)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Instances</b>: search-instances (QueryDescendants selectors), get-descendants-tree, get-game-info, get-nil-instances, get-instance-properties (every property, attribute and tag of one instance, hidden ones included), get-tagged (find CollectionService-tagged instances), get-property (one property), list-players (team, health, position)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Automation</b>: fire-remote (fire a RemoteEvent/RemoteFunction by path), set-property, call-method. Act on the game without writing Luau</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Memory</b>: gc-scan (filtergc the game's GC for tables or functions, matched by keys, values, constants or upvalues), get-env (dump getgenv / getrenv / getreg)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Scripts</b>: get-script-content (native decompile), script-grep (search the decompiled sources), get-script-strings (string literals read straight out of the bytecode, for scripts that will not decompile)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Script index</b>: build-script-index decompiles the whole game once and keeps it in memory. script-grep then answers instantly, covers every script, and takes regular expressions. It also unlocks find-remote-callers (traces a remote to the lines that fire it) and search-scripts (ranks scripts against a plain description like "where are purchases handled")</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Console</b>: get-console-output (read the Roblox developer console)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Remote spy</b>: remote-spy (list, block or ignore intercepted FireServer and InvokeServer calls)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Input</b>: send-input (real keyboard and mouse: keys, clicks, absolute and relative moves, scroll), type-text-box, click-button</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Screenshot</b>: screenshot-window (PNG of the Roblox window), list-roblox-windows</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Files</b>: read-file, write-file, list-files (Workspace / Scripts / AutoExec)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Game knowledge</b>: remember-game, game-feedback, recall-game-memory, forget-game-memory. Findings are saved per game and summarised back into get-game-info, so the next session starts where the last left off</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Runtime</b>: list-connections (which closures a signal actually runs), dump-anticheat-hooks (is the DataModel metatable hooked, and where), list-special-instances (nil-parented objects, running scripts, Actors), spy-closure (hook a live function and record what it is called with), dump-visible-ui (every GUI element the player can actually see, with paths you can act on)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Iterating</b>: live-reload (re-run an edited script without stacking a second copy; the previous run's listeners are torn down first and a STATE table survives the reload)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Real app</b>: open-script (save a script into Scripts/MCP and open it as an editor tab), launch-roblox (start the Roblox version Real supports)</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Checking</b>: check-script type-checks and lints Luau with the same analyzer as the editor, before code is run or saved. open-script runs it automatically and returns the findings</li> <li><b class="svelte-cbmkf3">Editor</b>: get-diagnostics (the Problems panel for your open tabs), get-app-log (the Real terminal)</li></ul></section></div>`);function iU(c,e){De(e,!0);let a=f(!1);Ta(()=>$t("mcp-open-docs",()=>{i(a,!0),wn.refresh()},window));const s=ie(()=>wn.status==="running"),l=ie(()=>wn.url||"http://127.0.0.1:3872/mcp"),d=ie(()=>wn.token||"<start the server to reveal your token>"),g=ie(()=>wn.stdioCommand||"<install a Real update to get the relay>"),h=ie(()=>JSON.stringify({mcpServers:{real:{command:t(g),args:[]}}},null,2));async function m(C,k){C&&(await Un(C)?We.success(`${k} copied`):We.error(`Could not copy ${k.toLowerCase()}`))}nn(c,{get open(){return t(a)},title:"Real MCP",subtitle:"Let an AI client write and run scripts through Real",width:"min(580px, calc(100vw - 32px))",onClose:()=>i(a,!1),icon:k=>{tt(k,{name:"lucide:server",size:20})},children:(k,T)=>{var A=sU(),w=r(A);{var L=he=>{var ce=aU();u(he,ce)};y(w,he=>{t(s)||he(L)})}var B=o(w,4),I=r(B),x=r(I);tt(x,{name:"lucide:link-2",size:13}),qe(),n(I);var S=o(I,8);{var _=he=>{var ce=nU(),re=r(ce);tt(re,{name:"lucide:alert-triangle",size:12}),qe(),n(ce),u(he,ce)};y(S,he=>{t(s)&&!wn.stdioAvailable&&he(_)})}n(B);var j=o(B,2),N=r(j),Y=r(N);tt(Y,{name:"lucide:terminal",size:13}),qe(),n(N);var F=o(N,4),M=r(F),R=r(M,!0);n(M);var p=o(M,2),E=r(p);tt(E,{name:"lucide:copy",size:12}),n(p),n(F);var U=o(F,4),z=r(U),G=r(z,!0);n(z);var ee=o(z,2),W=r(ee);tt(W,{name:"lucide:copy",size:12}),n(ee),n(U);var te=o(U,2);{var V=he=>{var ce=rU(),re=r(ce);tt(re,{name:"lucide:alert-triangle",size:12}),qe(),n(ce),u(he,ce)};y(te,he=>{t(s)&&!wn.stdioAvailable&&he(V)})}var O=o(te,4),Q=r(O),K=r(Q,!0);n(Q);var ae=o(Q,2),oe=r(ae);tt(oe,{name:"lucide:copy",size:12}),n(ae),n(O);var fe=o(O,2),me=r(fe),Z=r(me,!0);n(me);var X=o(me,2),$=r(X);tt($,{name:"lucide:copy",size:12}),n(X),n(fe),qe(2),n(j);var D=o(j,2),J=r(D),pe=r(J);tt(pe,{name:"lucide:shield",size:13}),qe(),n(J),qe(2),n(D);var ge=o(D,2),le=r(ge),ve=r(le);tt(ve,{name:"lucide:server",size:13}),qe(),n(le),qe(4),n(ge),n(A),q(()=>{ne(R,t(g)),ne(G,t(h)),ne(K,t(l)),ne(Z,t(d))})